 "text": "9/29/26, 9:47 AM\n\nTOU exception responses can only be archived if the respective billing document, whose billing period is found during the\nperiod for the corresponding TOU exception, has been archived.\n\ne Write temporary index:\n\nThe system writes the contract and the TOU exception program to the index table ETOUEXCEPTRESPAR for the TOU\nexception responses that can be archived. This index table is used as the basis for archiving. Once data has been\nsuccessfully archived and deleted, the system deletes the respective index entry from the database.\n\n2. Archiving of Selected TOU Exception Responses (Report REAARCH_ARCH_EXRESP)\n\nPrerequisite\n\nBefore starting this archiving report, you must perform at least one analysis using the REAARCH_ANALYSE_EXRESP report.\n\nProcess Flow\n\nThe archiving report selects TOU exception responses for which a corresponding entry exists in the index table\nETOUEXCEPTRESPAR, whose entries are generated by the analysis report. The system writes the entries found to the archive.\n\n1 Note\n\nIf you start the report in the test mode, the system does not write the data to the archive, and only displays an overview of the\ndocuments you can archive (if a detailed log display is required).\n\nWhen you start the report you can make various settings on the initial screen:\n\ne Log type: General statistical data, detail log with detailed data for each analyzed record or detail log with detailed data for\ndocuments that could not be archived.\n\ne Test run: If you start the report as a test run, no data is written to the database.\n\ne Comment on archive run: Here you can enter an individual comment for an archiving run.\n\nIn variant maintenance for the write program, the following actions from SAP NetWeaver Information Lifecycle Management are\navailable to you:\n\ne Archiving\n\nYou can use this action to archive data for completed business objects. The system performs archivability checks to\nestablish whether data can be archived. In this regard, this function is the same as standard data archiving. The ILM\nenhancements mean that during the write phase, the system can evaluate the rules maintained in the Information\nRetention Manager (IRM) for each object instance and therefore determine the retention period and the storage location\nfor the object. This information is persisted to the database as part of the administration data and is interpreted later\nduring storage.\n\ne Snapshots\n\nSnapshots are archiving sessions that are used to extract data from the database. This data is not deleted from the\ndatabase. The system does not execute any additional checks other than checking the restrictions in the selection variant.\nYou can use this option to write data to the archive from current, open business transactions. To prevent data from being\nlost, this type of session is not provided for data deletion. Therefore, snapshots always create redundant copies of data\nfrom the database. The snapshot function is mainly intended for use in conjunction with the ILM Retention Warehouse\n\nee De\n",
